  "Question": "When the fraction \\(\\dfrac{49}{84}\\) is expressed in simplest form, then the sum of the numerator and the denominator will be",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(11\\)",
    "B": "\\(17\\)",
    "C": "\\(19\\)",
    "D": "\\(33\\)",
    "E": "\\(133\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Both \\(49\\) and \\(84\\) are divisible by \\(7\\). Dividing the numerator and denominator by the same nonzero number preserves the fraction's value, so\n\\[\\frac{49}{84}=\\frac{49\\div7}{84\\div7}=\\frac7{12}.\\]\nThe only positive factors of \\(7\\) are \\(1\\) and \\(7\\), and \\(7\\) does not divide \\(12\\). Thus \\(\\frac7{12}\\) is in simplest form. The requested sum is \\(7+12=19\\), choice \\(\\mathrm C\\).",
